d  complete  lunacy now coverage of this event if you  compare it to other events  has been unfortunately the worst of the  worst that we could get from right wing  media  and even from so-called uh not  independent media from so-called  nonpartisan media  remember for example um  that the jacob blake story  was widely reported on just a couple of  days prior  and if you look at for example two new  york post tweets which we are putting up  on the screen for you on the left the  new york post tweeting about jacob blake  who was killed by police  jacob blake had a knife in his car when  he was shot by police  on the right the same new york post  with a picture of kyle rittenhouse  cleaning graffiti tweets suspected  teen gunman kyle rittenhouse  spotted cleaning kenosha graffiti before  the shooting now no mention of the fact  that  in wisconsin the minimum age to open  carry  is 18 so shooting aside  what kyle rittenhouse was doing was  against the law but of course  i guess nobody stopped him to say hey  what state are you from  and what age are you and is it even  legal for you to be here with this gun  remember that when trayvon martin was  killed by george zimmerman he was 17  years old  corporate media of course the right was  very quick to immediately say  he was 17 but this this guy was an adult  he was a big aggressive guy  and he's really an adult and he should  have he should be considered one in his  interaction with george zimmerman and  yet here  you have a gun-toting 17-year-old white  kid  also 17 uh at like trayvon martin  but this one's a kid who was cleaning  graffiti and anyway like tucker carlson  says  if the streets are out of control isn't  it natural for gun-toting 17-year-olds  to be out there policing  this is crazy this is crazy now we have  now  retrospectively found out that this kid  kyle rittenhouse i i maybe shouldn't  even be saying this kid he's 17 and  you know the legal system will determine  how he should be he should be dealt with  uh about two hours before the first  shooting  um he was actually interviewed written  house was  at a kenosha vehicle dealership by some  guy who was live streaming what was  going on in kenosha take a look at this  we're protecting from the citizens and i  just got pepper sprayed by a  person in the crowd so you had  non-weasel but  you just respond we don't have  non-lethal  so you guys are full-on ready to defend  the property yes we are  now if i can ask can you guys step back  medical ems right here  then we had another interview with kyle  rittenhouse who spoke to  richie mcginnis who's a video editor at  the daily caller a right-wing news and  opinion site  and again just stumbling across this  gun-toting 17 year old take a look what  are you doing out here obviously you're  armed and uh you're in front of this  business we saw burning last night so  what's up so people  are getting injured and our job is to  protect this business and part of my job  is also help people if there's somebody  hurt  i'm running into harm's way that's why i  have my rifle because i need to protect  myself  obviously now  i i think that there's a few different  things there's a bunch of stories here  one story as i've already pointed out  is the immediate media narratives that  are created  white kid with the gun it's just a kid  it's natural that he was out there he's  a good kid he was cleaning graffiti etc  uh even jacob blake immediately  oh well there was a knife in his car  did was that did police know that at the  time uh there's you know  claims about well there was a there was  a phone call the police may have  suspected et cetera but the handling of  these two  is completely different and that's one  storyline  the other storyline is this broader  narrative aside from this particular  case  it's the broader narrative of  republicans for months now have been  harping on  the streets are out of control joe biden  wants to defund the police which he  doesn't  everythin